# Rust build output. note-collab-sdk (a workspace member) builds into the
# repo-root /target; the excluded mobile-sdk crate builds into its own
# crates/mobile-sdk/target. Neither should ever be committed.
/target
crates/*/target

# build-android.sh output: the .so files + Kotlin bindings it produces are
# build artifacts, staged here for copying into the Android apps.
/build

# note-collab-sdk's locally generated bindings are a staging artifact — the
# authoritative copies live in note-android (Kotlin) and note-ios (Swift). (The
# mobile-sdk crate intentionally tracks its own crates/mobile-sdk/bindings, so
# that path is deliberately not ignored.)
crates/note-collab-sdk/bindings
